  {
   "id": "-TRe5Up0AQAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2020-04-18T00:19:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: [poppr] Import multi loci SSR data to poppr",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hello Javed,<div><br></div><div>I think I see the issue here. You do not need to assign a column for each observed allele. The genalex format assumes the number of loci multiplied by the ploidy. If you have a tetraploid, then you should have four columns per locus. The LU-1 locus is in the correct format, but the other loci all have five allele slots represented. Please take a look at the Polyploids section of the manual for details: <a href=\"https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_Preparation.html#polyploids\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_Preparation.html%23polyploids&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480277909000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZgqNd3ueeSm3GSzYSi0uT\">https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Data_Preparation.html#polyploids</a> </div><div><br></div><div>Additionally, please make sure the header and population information is formatted correctly. </div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps,</div><div>Zhian</div><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Apr 15, 2020, at 22:17 , Javed Akhtar &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">akhtar...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
